WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.250
Farming began about 12,000
to 11,000 years ago,

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.970
at the end of the most recent ice age.

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.790
High in the Andes, the cultivated potato
traces back to a single domestication,

4
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.410
in Peru.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.050
Once it first appeared
outside South America,

6
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.810
it rapidly diffused worldwide.

7
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.490
So how did crops spread from where
farming began to the rest of the world?

8
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.610
All at once?

9
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.770
On the wind, with the birds?

10
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.230
In this mission, you'll map where key
crops and animals were first domesticated,

11
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.110
and date them.

12
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.970
Then you'll follow crops
across mountains and oceans,

13
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:39.190
and see how the potato reached the world.

14
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:44.280
Your mission: explain how crops spread
from where farming began to the world.
